Ahead of their Fourth of July weekend wedding, Swift and Kelce pledged $26 million to charities across the United States, including the Grammy Museum Foundation, New York Cares, Harvesters in Kansas City, and Parton&#8217;s Imagination Library.

&#8220;Taylor and Travis, it&#8217;s Dolly,&#8221; Parton began in her video message to the soon-to-be-married couple. &#8220;I was just told that you two are making a donation of $2 million to my Imagination Library. Thank you, thank you, thank you! I&#8217;m blown away and overjoyed with that gratitude.&#8221;

View this post on Instagram

She added, &#8220;Now, it&#8217;s evident that you two have made giving back a key part of your lives. So, hey, when you have your first born, can I have it? Because that is gonna be one special baby!&#8221;

Parton went on to highlight the mission of her Dollywood Foundation — to &#8220;dream more, care more, learn more, and be more&#8221; — and said Swift and Kelce&#8217;s contribution will &#8220;continue that mission even in bigger ways.&#8221;

She closed the video by singing a snippet of her 1974 classic &#8220;I Will Always Love You.&#8221;

News of Swift and Kelce&#8217;s $26 million in charitable donations was announced earlier this week. On Thursday (July 2), the 14-time Grammy winner&#8217;s representative shared a list of organizations receiving contributions from the couple.

Many of the beneficiaries are located in places that hold personal significance for Swift and Kelce, including Reading, Pennsylvania, and Cleveland — their respective hometowns — as well as Nashville and Kansas City, where they built their careers. They also donated to several New York City-based organizations ahead of their wedding celebration, which is set to take place Friday (July 3) at Madison Square Garden.
